e5** because it:\n- Occupies the center with tempo\n- Opens diagonals for my f8 bishop and d8 queen\n- Establishes a strong pawn presence\n- Follows classical opening principles (control the center before attacking the flanks)\n- Doesn't create any weaknesses in my position\n- Punishes White's time-wasting flank move by gaining central space\n\nAnswer: P: e7-e5"}
