eason: B: c5-f2 delivers check and exploits White's awkward king position. Since White has already moved the king to f1 and lost castling rights, this forcing move creates immediate problems. After the king moves, I can continue development while maintaining pressure. This is more forcing than quiet developing moves and takes advantage of White's structural weaknesses.\n\nAnswer: B: c5-f2"}
