 **N: f6-g4+** is the strongest move because it forces White's king to move immediately (since it's check). The White king is already on f2, away from its usual safe position, and this check disrupts White's coordination while my knight can continue to harass. After Kg1 or Kg3, I maintain pressure and can follow up with castling or further development with tempo. This tactical shot is superior to the slower, positional alternatives.\n\nAnswer: N: f6-g4"}
