s forces White's king to move.\n\nReason: **N: f3-e5** delivers check to the White king on f5. This is the most forcing move available - it puts immediate pressure on White's exposed king and forces White to respond to the check. After the king moves, I can continue my attack with my well-placed pieces. In chess, checking the opponent's king is generally strong when their king is exposed, and f5 is definitely an exposed position for White's king.\n\nAnswer: N: f3-e5"}
