ctical blow that wins the initiative and puts White in serious trouble.\n\nReason: N: e5-d3 delivers check to the exposed White king on f5, which is an unnatural and vulnerable square for a king. This forces White's king to move immediately, and I gain tempo while improving my knight's position. The knight on d3 would be excellently placed, controlling key central squares and potentially winning material in the follow-up. This is clearly the strongest move tactically.\n\nAnswer: N: e5-d3"}
