son: The move e3-e2 is overwhelmingly the strongest option. A pawn on the 2nd rank is extremely dangerous - White must respond to prevent queening, which will give me either a queen (winning material advantage) or at minimum force White into a desperate defensive position. This is a classic case of "passed pawns must be pushed."\n\nAnswer: P: e3-e2'}
