s not a valid knight move (it's only 2 squares horizontally). The rook on a1 cannot reach e1 either. White's bishop on a2 cannot reach e1. This promotion appears safe!\n\nReason: Promoting my pawn to a queen on e2-e1 is clearly the best move. It gains overwhelming material advantage (a queen is worth approximately 9 points). After promotion, I'll have a queen deep in White's position that cannot be immediately captured, giving me a winning advantage. This is a forcing, concrete move that capitalizes on my advanced passed pawn.\n\nAnswer: P: e2-e1-q"}
