vantage and removes a defensive piece near White's King.\n\nReason: Capturing the Knight on h3 with my Queen is the strongest move because:\n- It wins material immediately (a whole Knight)\n- My Queen remains active and threatening\n- It further weakens White's already vulnerable King position\n- There's no apparent tactical drawback to this capture\n- With my existing material advantage, simplifying while maintaining the advantage is the correct strategy\n\nAnswer: Q: h1-h3"}
