ontrols key squares, very aggressive\n- **N: f2-e4**: Solid centralization\n\nReason: **Q: h1-h5+** is the strongest move because:\n1. It gives check, forcing White's King to move from its already exposed position on f5\n2. The King has limited escape squares (likely e6, f6, g6, e4, or g4)\n3. After the King moves, I can continue pressing my advantage with my well-coordinated pieces\n4. It maintains the initiative and keeps White on the defensive\n5. With my material advantage (Queen + Knight vs scattered pieces), forcing moves that restrict the opponent's options are optimal\n\nAnswer: Q: h1-h5"}
