t to move (likely Kf2 or Ke2). This check restricts White's options, keeps my rook active on the back rank, and maintains complete control of the position. After the king moves, I can continue to harass it while advancing my pawns or targeting White's remaining pawns. This is the most forcing and effective continuation.\n\nAnswer: R: d2-d1"}
